questions.question:
"Café au lait" is sent as UTF-8. The "é" is two bytes (0xC3 0xA9), and the network delivers chunk 1 = "Caf" + 0xC3 and chunk 2 = 0xA9 + " au lait". The client runs:

const decoder = new TextDecoder();
let text = '';
for (const chunk of [chunk1, chunk2]) text += decoder.decode(chunk);

What is text?
